%!PS
% Test content for process.ps: the most steps (eight), lines near their limit, a
% long path back between two late steps; blueprint theme.
% `psanim check process-parcel.ps` runs process.ps with it.
/tpl (process.ps) component
/film /tpl << /Params <<
  /look /blueprint
  /heading (How a parcel crosses the country in two days)
  /steps [
    [ (order) (A customer pays, and the shop prints a picking list for it.) ]
    [ (pick) (A worker walks the shelves and collects every item on it.) ]
    [ (pack) (The items are boxed, padded and weighed on a scale.) ]
    [ (label) (A barcode label records the address and the weight.) ]
    [ (collect) (A van takes the day's parcels to the regional depot.) ]
    [ (sort) (Scanners read each label and route the box to a truck.) ]
    [ (carry) (Overnight trucks drive the boxes to the local depots.) ]
    [ (deliver) (A courier brings the parcel to the door and takes a photo.) ]
  ]
  /key 5
  /why (One misread label here sends a parcel to the wrong end of the country.)
  /loop [ 7 5 (nobody at home) (If nobody answers, the parcel goes back to be sorted again.) ]
  /summary (Eight hands, one label, and a sorting machine in the middle.)
>> >> instance
<< /Size [1280 720] /Duration /film componentduration /FPS 30 >> animation
/scene { /film << /After /hold >> place } def
